@* Behaviours (UI docs): dnf.js - progressive enhancement, the dnfUI API and every data-* hook, live where practical. *@

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>Script <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/wwwroot/dnf.js</code></li>
    <li>Served at <code>/_content/DotNetForge.UI/dnf.js</code></li>
</ul>

<p><code>dnf.js</code> is one small, dependency-free script, loaded with <code>defer</code> after the stylesheet
    (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/installation#assets">Using the library</a>). It wires <code>data-*</code> hooks in the
    markup and exposes <code>window.dnfUI</code>. Whatever state it changes is written as attributes -
    <code>aria-expanded</code>, <code>data-open</code>, <code>data-selected</code> … - which the CSS styles
    (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization#states">States</a>).</p>

<h2 id="progressive">Progressive enhancement</h2>
<p>Every screen must work without JavaScript: forms post, links navigate, <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> opens, tabs show
    all their panels stacked, and a form with a confirmation submits directly. The script only adds convenience -
    client-side search, filters, sorting, paging, the theme switch and bulk selection need it, so every bulk action
    should also exist per item. Two ways to hide controls that only work with JavaScript:</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Mechanism</th><th>Shown</th><th>Use for</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>hidden data-js-only</code></td><td>when <code>dnf.js</code> runs (deferred - after the first paint)</td><td>search boxes, view switches, copy buttons</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>class="dnf-js-only"</code></td><td>from the first paint (<code>dnf-theme.js</code> marks <code>&lt;html class="dnf-js"&gt;</code> in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>)</td><td>controls that must not pop in late, like the theme menu</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="csp">Content Security Policy</h2>
<p>Nothing needs <code>unsafe-inline</code>: no inline script, no <code>style</code> attribute in markup, no event-handler
    attributes. Configuration travels in <code>data-*</code> attributes, and the text of dialogs and toasts is set with
    <code>textContent</code>. The script positions floating panels (<code>style.top</code>, <code>style.left</code>) and
    the tooltip's arrow (a custom property) through the CSSOM, which <code>style-src 'self'</code> allows.</p>

<h2 id="api">The dnfUI API</h2>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Member</th><th>Does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnfUI.toast(message, tone)</code></td><td>shows a toast. <code>tone</code>: <code>"success"</code>, <code>"info"</code> (also for anything unknown), <code>"warning"</code> or <code>"danger"</code>. A danger toast stays until dismissed (<code>role="alert"</code>); the others hide after 6 seconds (<code>role="status"</code>). Needs the <a href="#toasts">toast region and template</a>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnfUI.confirm({ title, text, action, tone })</code></td><td>opens the <a href="#confirm">confirmation dialog</a> and returns a <code>Promise&lt;boolean&gt;</code>. <code>tone: "primary"</code> for a non-destructive question (danger otherwise). Without the dialog or <code>showModal</code> it falls back to <code>window.confirm(text)</code>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnfUI.init(root)</code></td><td>wires the per-element behaviours - tabs, collections, view switches, file uploads, frames, <code>data-js-only</code>, check groups, theme buttons, server toasts - inside markup added after load. Each behaviour runs once per element.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnfUI.icon(name, size, className)</code></td><td>the markup of a decorative sprite icon. <code>size</code>: <code>"sm"</code>, <code>"lg"</code>, <code>"xl"</code> or omitted; <code>className</code>: extra classes. Nothing is encoded - pass known icon ids and class names only.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<ui-doc-code id="api-js" lang="js">
// A toast: "success", "info" (the default), "warning" or "danger".
dnfUI.toast("Page published.", "success");

// A question: resolves to true when the user confirms.
const confirmed = await dnfUI.confirm({
    title: "Delete webhook",
    text: "Deliveries to this URL stop immediately.",
    action: "Delete",
    tone: "danger"
});

// Markup added after load: wire its per-element behaviours.
panel.innerHTML = html;
dnfUI.init(panel);

// The markup of a sprite icon: name, size, extra classes.
button.innerHTML = dnfUI.icon("trash", "sm", "dnf-button__icon") + "Delete";
</ui-doc-code>

<p>The delegated behaviours - dropdowns, tooltips, dialogs, confirm, pending, copy, reveal, fill, the drawer and the theme
    switch - listen on the document, so they work for added markup without <code>init</code>.</p>

<h2 id="dropdowns">Dropdowns and popovers</h2>
<p>Menus and popovers are native popovers: a <code>&lt;button popovertarget="id"&gt;</code> and a panel with
    <code>popover</code>. The browser opens the panel in the top layer and closes it on Escape and on outside clicks.
    For <code>.dnf-dropdown__menu[popover]</code> and <code>.dnf-popover[popover]</code>, <code>dnf.js</code> adds:</p>
<ul>
    <li>placement next to the opener from <code>data-placement</code> - <code>bottom-end</code> (default),
        <code>bottom-start</code>, <code>top-end</code>, <code>top-start</code> - flipped when there is no room, kept 8px
        inside the window and placed again on scroll and resize;</li>
    <li><code>aria-expanded</code> on the opener and <code>data-open</code> on the panel while it is open;</li>
    <li>for a menu opened from the keyboard: focus on the first item, ArrowDown and ArrowUp (wrapping), Home and End; a
        click on an item closes the menu.</li>
</ul>

<ui-doc-example id="dropdown-demo" title="A menu and a popover" description="The tag helper renders the menu markup; a popover is a plain panel with popover and data-placement.">
    <dnf-dropdown label="Actions for report.pdf" variant="Secondary" size="Md">
        <dnf-dropdown-label>report.pdf</dnf-dropdown-label>
        <dnf-dropdown-button icon="pencil" data-docs-toast="Rename - a demo, nothing changed.">Rename</dnf-dropdown-button>
        <dnf-dropdown-button icon="link" data-copy-text="https://example.com/media/report.pdf">Copy link</dnf-dropdown-button>
        <dnf-dropdown-separator />
        <dnf-dropdown-button icon="trash" danger="true" data-docs-confirm="report.pdf is removed from the media library." data-docs-confirm-title="Delete file" data-docs-confirm-action="Delete">Delete</dnf-dropdown-button>
    </dnf-dropdown>
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--outline" popovertarget="docs-publish-popover" aria-expanded="false">Why can't I publish?</button>
    <div class="dnf-popover" id="docs-publish-popover" popover data-placement="bottom-start">
        <p class="text-sm">Publishing needs a role with the publish permission. Ask an administrator to change your role.</p>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<p>Prefer <code>&lt;dnf-dropdown&gt;</code> (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/dropdown">Dropdown</a>) for menus;
    popover panels: <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/popover">Popover</a>.</p>

<h2 id="tooltips">Tooltips</h2>
<p><code>data-tooltip="Text"</code> on a focusable element. One shared <code>.dnf-tooltip</code> (<code>role="tooltip"</code>,
    a manual popover) shows on hover and on keyboard focus, above the element or below it when there is no room, centred
    and kept inside the window. It hides on mouse-out, blur, scroll, pointer down and Escape. Give the element the same
    text as its accessible name - without JavaScript that is all there is.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="tooltip-demo" title="Tooltips" description="Hover or tab to a button. Each one's aria-label names it; the tooltip shows the same words.">
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary dnf-button--icon-only" aria-label="Duplicate" data-tooltip="Duplicate"><dnf-icon name="copy" class="dnf-button__icon" /></button>
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary dnf-button--icon-only" aria-label="Download" data-tooltip="Download"><dnf-icon name="download" class="dnf-button__icon" /></button>
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary dnf-button--icon-only" aria-label="Settings" data-tooltip="Settings"><dnf-icon name="settings" class="dnf-button__icon" /></button>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="tabs">Tabs</h2>
<p>A <code>[data-tabs]</code> root with <code>button[role=tab][data-tab]</code> tabs and <code>[data-tab-panel]</code>
    panels. The root gets <code>data-tabbed="true"</code> and one panel shows at a time; tabs get
    <code>aria-selected</code> and a roving <code>tabindex</code>; ArrowLeft and ArrowRight (wrapping), Home and End move
    between them.</p>
<ul>
    <li>The open tab is written to the URL hash (<code>#seo</code>), so a reload or a redirect to <code>…#seo</code>
        reopens it. The first tab shown: the hash, else <code>data-initial-tab</code>, else the first tab, already at the
        first paint.</li>
    <li><code>data-tab-hash="false"</code> on the root neither reads nor writes the hash - for many small tab groups on one
        page, like the example below and the example frames of these docs.</li>
    <li>Inside a form, a field with <code>data-tab-field</code> receives the open tab's name, and a field that fails
        native validation on a hidden tab opens its tab.</li>
    <li>A root manages only its own tabs and panels: a panel may hold another tab group.</li>
</ul>

<ui-doc-example id="tabs-demo" title="Tabs" description="Without JavaScript the three panels show one below the other, each with its title." layout="block">
