<h2 id="dialogs">Dialogs</h2>
<p><code>data-dialog-open="&lt;selector&gt;"</code> opens that <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> with <code>showModal()</code>: focus
    moves in, Escape closes it and the page behind is inert. <code>data-dialog-close</code> closes the dialog it is in (so
    does a button of a <code>&lt;form method="dialog"&gt;</code>, which also sets <code>returnValue</code>);
    <code>data-dialog-light-dismiss</code> on the dialog closes it on a click on the backdrop.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="dialog-demo" title="A dialog" description="Open it, then close it with Cancel, the close button, Escape or a click on the backdrop.">
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" data-dialog-open="#docs-new-folder"><dnf-icon name="folder" class="dnf-button__icon" /> New folder</button>
    <dialog class="dnf-dialog dnf-dialog--sm" id="docs-new-folder" aria-labelledby="docs-new-folder-title" aria-describedby="docs-new-folder-text" data-dialog-light-dismiss>
        <div class="dnf-dialog__header">
            <span class="dnf-dialog__icon"><dnf-icon name="folder" /></span>
            <div>
                <h2 class="dnf-dialog__title" id="docs-new-folder-title">New folder</h2>
                <p class="dnf-dialog__description" id="docs-new-folder-text">Folders group media; files keep their URLs.</p>
            </div>
            <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--ghost dnf-button--sm dnf-button--icon-only dnf-dialog__close" aria-label="Close" data-dialog-close><dnf-icon name="x" size="Sm" /></button>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-dialog__body">
            <div class="dnf-field">
                <label class="dnf-field__label" for="docs-folder-name">Name</label>
                <input class="dnf-input" id="docs-folder-name" value="Brochures" />
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-dialog__footer">
            <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" data-dialog-close>Cancel</button>
            <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--primary" data-dialog-close data-docs-toast="Folder created - a demo, nothing was saved." data-docs-toast-tone="success">Create</button>
        </div>
    </dialog>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="drawer">Drawer navigation</h2>
<p><code>[data-drawer-open]</code> sets <code>data-nav-open="true"</code> on the first <code>[data-shell]</code> of the page,
    shows every <code>[data-drawer-backdrop]</code>, sets <code>aria-expanded</code> and focuses the panel's
    <code>a[aria-current]</code> (else its first link). <code>[data-drawer-close]</code>, Escape and a window at least
    <code>64.0625rem</code> wide close it and return focus to the open button. The library has no drawer CSS: the layout
    styles <code>[data-nav-open="true"]</code> - the admin shell does, and so does the navigation of these docs on a narrow
    window.</p>

<ui-doc-code id="drawer-markup" lang="html">
<div data-shell>
    <nav data-drawer-panel>
        …
        <button type="button" data-drawer-close aria-label="Close navigation">…</button>
    </nav>
    <div data-drawer-backdrop data-drawer-close hidden></div>
    <button type="button" data-drawer-open aria-expanded="false" aria-label="Open navigation">…</button>
</div>
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="scroll">Scroll position after a POST</h2>
<p>When a <code>method="post"</code> form is submitted (and not cancelled), the URL and the scroll position are kept in
    <code>sessionStorage</code>. If the next page has the same path and query within 30 seconds, it scrolls back once
    every deferred script has run - so a screen that posts and redirects back to itself stays where it was. Links,
    reloads and Back are untouched. Nothing to add to the markup.</p>

<h2 id="toasts">Toasts</h2>
<p><code>dnfUI.toast</code> clones the template's first element, adds <code>dnf-toast--&lt;tone&gt;</code>, sets the role,
    the message and the icon (<code>circle-check</code>, <code>circle-x</code>, <code>info</code> or
    <code>triangle-alert</code>), and appends it to <code>[data-toasts]</code>. Toasts the server rendered into the region
    are inserted again on load, so screen readers announce them. <code>data-autohide="true"</code> removes a toast after
    6 seconds unless it is hovered or focused; <code>[data-toast-close]</code> dismisses it.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="toast-demo" title="Toasts" description="One button per tone. These buttons call dnfUI.toast through a demo hook of the docs.">
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" data-docs-toast="Page published." data-docs-toast-tone="success">Success</button>
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" data-docs-toast="Import started - you can leave this screen." data-docs-toast-tone="info">Info</button>
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" data-docs-toast="The webhook took 8 seconds to answer." data-docs-toast-tone="warning">Warning</button>
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" data-docs-toast="The upload failed: the file is larger than 20 MB." data-docs-toast-tone="danger">Danger</button>
</ui-doc-example>

<p>The region and the template, once per layout (CMS layouts render them with <code>&lt;partial name="_Feedback" /&gt;</code>):</p>

<ui-doc-code id="toast-markup" lang="html">
<div class="dnf-toast-region" data-toasts aria-live="polite">
    <!-- toasts rendered by the server: data-toast (+ data-autohide="true") -->
</div>
<template id="dnf-toast-template">
    <div class="dnf-toast" role="status" data-toast>
        <svg class="dnf-icon dnf-toast__icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="/_content/DotNetForge.UI/icons.svg#info"></use></svg>
        <p class="dnf-toast__message"></p>
        <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--ghost dnf-button--sm dnf-button--icon-only" data-toast-close
                aria-label="Dismiss">…</button>
    </div>
</template>
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="confirm">Confirmation dialog</h2>
<p>On submit of a form with <code>data-confirm</code> - or through a submit button that carries the
    <code>data-confirm*</code> attributes itself - the submit is cancelled, the dialog asks, and Yes submits again with
    the same submitter. Without JavaScript the form submits directly.</p>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>data-confirm</code></td><td>the question</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-confirm-title</code></td><td>the dialog's title; default "Are you sure?"</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-confirm-action</code></td><td>the OK button's text; default "Confirm"</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-confirm-tone</code></td><td><code>primary</code> for a non-destructive question; anything else is danger</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<ui-doc-example id="confirm-demo" title="Confirmations" description="A destructive and a non-destructive question. Nothing is deleted or published - the docs show the answer as a toast.">
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--danger-soft" data-docs-confirm="The page and its child pages are deleted." data-docs-confirm-title="Delete page" data-docs-confirm-action="Delete">Delete page</button>
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" data-docs-confirm="Visitors see the new version right away." data-docs-confirm-title="Publish now?" data-docs-confirm-action="Publish" data-docs-confirm-tone="primary">Publish</button>
</ui-doc-example>

<p>On a real form:</p>

<ui-doc-code id="confirm-form" lang="razor">
<form method="post" asp-action="Delete" asp-route-id="@@Model.Id" data-confirm="The page and its child pages are deleted."
      data-confirm-title="Delete page" data-confirm-action="Delete">
    <button type="submit" class="dnf-button dnf-button--danger-soft">Delete page</button>
</form>
</ui-doc-code>

<p>The dialog, once per layout (part of <code>_Feedback</code> in the CMS). The script replaces the OK button's and the
    icon's <code>className</code> on every call, so don't put other classes on them; the answer is
    <code>returnValue === "confirm"</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-code id="confirm-dialog-markup" lang="html">
<dialog class="dnf-dialog" id="dnf-confirm-dialog" aria-labelledby="confirm-title" aria-describedby="confirm-text">
    <form method="dialog">
        <div class="dnf-dialog__header">
            <span class="dnf-dialog__icon dnf-dialog__icon--danger" data-confirm-icon>…</span>
            <div>
                <h2 class="dnf-dialog__title" id="confirm-title" data-confirm-title>Are you sure?</h2>
                <p class="dnf-dialog__description" id="confirm-text" data-confirm-text></p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-dialog__footer">
            <button type="submit" value="cancel" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary">Cancel</button>
            <button type="submit" value="confirm" class="dnf-button dnf-button--danger" data-confirm-ok>Confirm</button>
        </div>
    </form>
</dialog>
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="pending">Pending on submit</h2>
<p><code>&lt;form data-pending-on-submit&gt;</code>: on a submit that was not cancelled, the submitter (else the first
    <code>[type=submit]</code>) gets <code>data-pending="true"</code> and <code>aria-busy="true"</code> - a
    <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/button#pending">button</a> shows its spinner and ignores further clicks until
    the next page loads.</p>

<ui-doc-code id="pending-form" lang="razor">
<form method="post" asp-action="Save" data-pending-on-submit>
    …
    <dnf-button variant="Primary" type="submit" icon="save">Save</dnf-button>
</form>
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="collections">Collections</h2>
<p>Client-side search, filters, sorting, paging and selection over the items already in the page - a table or a grid of
    cards. Try it: search, filter by type, sort a column, select rows.</p>

