                        <td>price-list.docx</td>
                        <td data-sort-value="64000">64 KB</td>
                        <td data-sort-value="2026-10-12">12 Oct 2026</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="dnf-empty-state dnf-empty-state--compact" data-collection-empty hidden>No file matches.</p>
        <div class="dnf-pagination" data-collection-pagination hidden></div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Hook</th><th>Behaviour</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>[data-collection]</code></td><td>the scope; the <code>[data-item]</code> elements inside are the items</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[data-collection-search]</code></td><td>an input: an item matches when its <code>data-search</code> (else its text) contains the query, ignoring case</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>select[data-collection-filter="key"]</code></td><td>an item matches when the select's value is one of the space-separated words of its <code>data-&lt;key&gt;</code>; an empty value is no filter</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>button[data-collection-filter="key"][data-value]</code></td><td>the same as exclusive toggle buttons: the clicked one gets <code>aria-pressed="true"</code>, the others with that key <code>"false"</code> - put them in a <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/segmented">segmented control</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>th[data-sort="text|number|date"]</code></td><td>becomes a <code>dnf-table__sort</code> button; a click sorts the rows of the first <code>tbody</code> by that column's <code>data-sort-value</code> (else its text) and toggles <code>aria-sort</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>data-page-size="N"</code> + <code>[data-collection-pagination]</code></td><td>paging; the pager is rendered into the element and shows once there are more than 10 items (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/pagination">Pagination</a>). Without <code>data-page-size</code> (or <code>0</code>) everything shows</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[data-collection-count]</code></td><td>"N total" or "X of N"</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[data-collection-empty]</code></td><td>shown when there are items and none matches</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[data-select-all]</code></td><td>checks every visible <code>[data-select-item]</code>; shows checked or indeterminate</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[data-select-item]</code></td><td>a selected item's <code>[data-item]</code> gets <code>data-selected="true"</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>[data-bulk-bar]</code>, <code>[data-bulk-count]</code>, <code>[data-bulk-clear]</code></td><td>the bar shows while something is selected ("N selected"); clear unchecks everything</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Search, filter and page-size changes go back to page 1. Item checkboxes post with <code>form="…"</code>, so they can
    live in the table while the bulk form is elsewhere on the page.</p>

<h2 id="view-switch">View switch</h2>
<p><code>[data-view-switch="name"]</code> with <code>[data-view-button]</code> buttons sets <code>data-view-mode</code> on
    the element named by <code>data-view-target</code> and <code>aria-pressed</code> on the buttons. The choice is
    remembered per switch in <code>localStorage</code>. The library has no <code>data-view-mode</code> CSS: the screen lays
    out the same items for each mode - here with a Tailwind <code>data-[view-mode=list]:</code> variant.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="view-switch-demo" title="Grid or list" description="One set of items, two layouts. Without JavaScript the switch stays hidden (hidden data-js-only)." layout="stack">
    <div class="dnf-segmented self-start" role="group" aria-label="View" data-view-switch="docs-media" data-view-target="#docs-view-items" data-default="grid" hidden data-js-only>
        <button type="button" class="dnf-segmented__item dnf-segmented__item--icon" data-view-button="grid" aria-label="Grid" data-tooltip="Grid"><dnf-icon name="grid" size="Sm" /></button>
        <button type="button" class="dnf-segmented__item dnf-segmented__item--icon" data-view-button="list" aria-label="List" data-tooltip="List"><dnf-icon name="list" size="Sm" /></button>
    </div>
    <div id="docs-view-items" class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-3 data-[view-mode=list]:grid-cols-1">
        <div class="dnf-card flex items-center gap-2 p-3 text-sm"><dnf-icon name="image" /> hero.jpg</div>
        <div class="dnf-card flex items-center gap-2 p-3 text-sm"><dnf-icon name="file" /> annual-report.pdf</div>
        <div class="dnf-card flex items-center gap-2 p-3 text-sm"><dnf-icon name="film" /> product-tour.mp4</div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="check-groups">Check-all groups</h2>
<p><code>&lt;input type="checkbox" data-check-group="name"&gt;</code> checks or clears every
    <code>[data-check-member="name"]</code>, and shows checked when all members are and indeterminate when some are - also
    on load.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="check-group-demo" title="A check-all group" description="Two of three members are checked, so the group starts indeterminate." layout="stack">
    <div class="dnf-check-list">
        <label class="dnf-check">
            <input type="checkbox" class="dnf-checkbox" data-check-group="docs-content" />
            <span class="dnf-check__text font-semibold">Content - every permission</span>
        </label>
        <div class="dnf-check-list ps-6">
            <label class="dnf-check"><input type="checkbox" class="dnf-checkbox" data-check-member="docs-content" checked /><span class="dnf-check__text">Read entries</span></label>
            <label class="dnf-check"><input type="checkbox" class="dnf-checkbox" data-check-member="docs-content" checked /><span class="dnf-check__text">Create and edit entries</span></label>
            <label class="dnf-check"><input type="checkbox" class="dnf-checkbox" data-check-member="docs-content" /><span class="dnf-check__text">Delete entries</span></label>
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="copy">Copy</h2>
<p><code>data-copy-text="value"</code>, or <code>data-copy-target="#id"</code> (an input's value, else the element's
    text), copies to the clipboard - trimmed - and shows a toast: "Copied to clipboard." or an error.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="copy-demo" title="Copy buttons" description="A copy action inside an input, and a button with its own text to copy.">
    <div class="dnf-input-group w-80">
        <input class="dnf-input" id="docs-copy-url" readonly value="https://example.com/api/content/articles" aria-label="Endpoint URL" />
        <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--ghost dnf-button--sm dnf-button--icon-only dnf-input-group__action" data-copy-target="#docs-copy-url" aria-label="Copy URL" data-tooltip="Copy URL"><dnf-icon name="copy" size="Sm" /></button>
    </div>
    <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary" data-copy-text="about-us"><dnf-icon name="copy" class="dnf-button__icon" /> Copy slug</button>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="reveal">Password reveal</h2>
<p><code>data-reveal="#id"</code> toggles the input between <code>password</code> and <code>text</code>, and toggles
    <code>aria-pressed</code>, the label ("Show password" or "Hide password") and which <code>[data-reveal-icon]</code> is
    hidden. Put the button in an <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/input-group">input group</a> as its action.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="reveal-demo" title="Show the password" description="The eye button reveals the value; its label and icon follow.">
    <div class="dnf-field w-72">
        <label class="dnf-field__label" for="docs-reveal-password">Password</label>
        <div class="dnf-input-group">
            <input class="dnf-input" type="password" id="docs-reveal-password" value="correct horse battery" autocomplete="off" />
            <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--ghost dnf-button--sm dnf-button--icon-only dnf-input-group__action" data-reveal="#docs-reveal-password" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Show password">
                <dnf-icon name="eye" size="Sm" data-reveal-icon="show" />
                <dnf-icon name="eye-off" size="Sm" data-reveal-icon="hide" hidden />
            </button>
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="file-upload">File upload</h2>
<p>On every <code>.dnf-file-upload</code> (wired by <code>init</code>): <code>data-dragging="true"</code> while files are
    dragged over it, and after a choice the file names are listed as primary badges in
    <code>[data-file-upload-files]</code> (<a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/components/file-upload">File upload</a>).</p>

<ui-doc-example id="file-upload-demo" title="Chosen files" description="Choose or drop files: their names appear below. Nothing is uploaded." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-file-upload">
        <input type="file" class="dnf-file-upload__input" multiple aria-label="Files to upload" aria-describedby="docs-upload-help" />
        <dnf-icon name="upload" size="Lg" />
        <p class="dnf-file-upload__title">Drop files here or click to choose</p>
        <p class="text-sm" id="docs-upload-help">Images, video, PDF - up to 20 MB each.</p>
        <div class="dnf-file-upload__files" data-file-upload-files></div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="fill">Fill a form</h2>
<p><code>data-fill="#form"</code> sets each named field of that form from the matching <code>data-fill-&lt;name&gt;</code>
    attribute, then focuses the form's first control - an "Edit" button on a row that loads the row into the form. HTML
    lower-cases attribute names, so it suits lower-case field names.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="fill-demo" title="Edit a row in a form" description="Each button fills the form with its row's values." layout="stack">
    <div class="dnf-cluster">
        <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary dnf-button--sm" data-fill="#docs-fill-form" data-fill-key="site.name" data-fill-value="DotNetForge">Edit site.name</button>
        <button type="button" class="dnf-button dnf-button--secondary dnf-button--sm" data-fill="#docs-fill-form" data-fill-key="site.tagline" data-fill-value="Content, forged.">Edit site.tagline</button>
    </div>
    <form id="docs-fill-form" class="dnf-form-grid" action="#fill">
        <div class="dnf-field">
            <label class="dnf-field__label" for="docs-fill-key">Key</label>
            <input class="dnf-input dnf-input--mono" id="docs-fill-key" name="key" />
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-field">
            <label class="dnf-field__label" for="docs-fill-value">Value</label>
            <input class="dnf-input" id="docs-fill-value" name="value" />
        </div>
    </form>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="frames">Frames</h2>
<p>An <code>&lt;iframe data-frame&gt;</code> inside a <code>[data-frame-host]</code>: the host gets
    <code>data-loaded="true"</code> once the frame has loaded (also when it already had). The host's own CSS decides what
    that changes - the CMS hides the skeleton of an extension's admin tab.</p>

<ui-doc-code id="frame-markup" lang="html">
<div data-frame-host>
    <div class="dnf-skeleton">…</div>
    <iframe data-frame src="…" title="Reports"></iframe>
</div>
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="theme">Theme switch</h2>
<p><code>[data-theme-set="light|dark|system"]</code> switches the theme on click and marks the checked choice -
    <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/theming#switching">Theming</a>.</p>

<h2 id="storage">Storage keys</h2>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Storage</th><th>Holds</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-theme</code></td><td><code>localStorage</code></td><td><code>light</code> or <code>dark</code>; absent means the system preference</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-page-size:&lt;path&gt;:&lt;index&gt;</code></td><td><code>localStorage</code></td><td>rows per page of the collection at that position of the screen</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-view:&lt;name&gt;</code></td><td><code>localStorage</code></td><td>the view of a <code>data-view-switch</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-scroll</code></td><td><code>sessionStorage</code></td><td>the scroll position of the last POST</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Blocked storage (a private window) is caught everywhere; the behaviour then falls back to its default.</p>
